# OpenMower OS: local Raspberry Pi firmware config overrides.
#
# Included at the end of config.txt (Pi firmware `include usercfg.txt`) --
# anything here overrides settings shipped in config.txt itself. config.txt
# is overwritten wholesale by every OS update; THIS file lives on /data and
# survives updates instead -- see openmower-sync-bootcfg (applies it live,
# on edit) and rauc-hook.sh (re-applies it to freshly installed OTA images).
#
# Edit this file directly on a running device (/data/boot/usercfg.txt), then
# reboot for it to take effect. One reboot is usually enough (an edit is
# applied to the active boot partition immediately, see
# openmower-sync-bootcfg.path) -- but config.txt itself is read by the Pi
# firmware before Linux even starts, so if your edit lands too late to be
# picked up before that reboot's firmware stage, the boot after it will.
#
# Example: switch the CM4 Wi-Fi antenna from internal (config.txt's default,
# dtparam=ant1) to an external U.FL/IPEX antenna:
#dtparam=ant2
